Triton 3.8.0, torch 2.11.0+cu130, NVIDIA L40

## Part 1: the accumulation window (one output element)
Row of `a`: products as listed, `b` all ones, `acc` as listed. `kept(t)`: the result minus the large term, in units of the small terms' sum (1 = every small term kept, 0 = all dropped).

| operands | path | K | small terms 2^-t against one term 1 (largest t kept fully) | K terms 1 against acc 2^s (largest s kept) | acc 1+2^-23, no products: result - 1 |
